  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish the exact alloy's FCC/L12–B2 lamellar architecture (R8, R16), show that annealing temperature can alter ordering or phase constitution in related HEAs (especially R2 and R19), and provide general links between ordering, dislocation resistance, stacking-fault behavior, and ductility (R5, R15, R17, R18, R20). Thus they could motivate temperature-dependent aging experiments. However, none identifies the specific 600°C maximum in L12 ordering and jagged boundary density, the APBE/cross-slip mechanism, or the ductile–brittle–ductile recovery at 750°C. Reconstructing those details would require a substantial new idea."
